{"title":"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be real numbers such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/7/747d227c5c93ab38b45ffe98794d68ac188986dd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(u + u^2 + u^3 + \\cdots + u^8) + 10u^9 = (v + v^2 + v^3 + \\cdots + v^{10}) + 10v^{11} = 8.\\]\" width=\"480\" height=\"19\" />\nDetermine, with proof, which of the two numbers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, is larger.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>We define real functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> as follows:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/5/1f5ec8e2b4de4d798c17a6493147af0a3b272f47.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} U(x) &amp;= (x+x^2 + \\dotsb + x^8) + 10x^9 = \\frac{x^{10}-x}{x-1} + 9x^9 \\\\ V(x) &amp;= (x+x^2 + \\dotsb + x^{10}) + 10x^{11} = \\frac{x^{12}-x}{x-1} + 9x^{11} . \\end{align*}\" width=\"426\" height=\"86\" />\nWe wish to show that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/7/7074ae0a95013a4f6045ac1b928149f0110af38e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U(u)=V(v)=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/7/ed7ffe0563c6df8b378ba45bf11c11e0c3f79c42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u &lt;v$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>We first note that when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/6/1b667f99b88cc4dd636e45b0cdf1bf965992738a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\le 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/e/cce24baa4db0ce59b69d97c7576c0120f35ad1af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{12}-x \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/d/14dd5bcd5d074df8011693f56cd0faa1362fe9bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-1 &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/0/43018098f9a03499b21d8adcc101ba68e7dbf3bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9x^9 \\le 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/b/a1b8d3aedf346b5aa699546e25156e20d990103d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[U(x) = \\frac{x^{10}-x}{x-1} + 9x^9 \\le 0 &lt; 8 .\\]\" width=\"242\" height=\"39\" />\nSimilarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/4/6445c800f83d07dc795bce8f22b5a0970f2b8829.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V(x) \\le 0 &lt; 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We also note that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/e/cdef99f026ca46b44a997cf5f8d85076428f2118.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\ge 9/10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />, then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/8/7b801995147880225d6c060cc681c033d06a980b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} U(x) &amp;= \\frac{x-x^{10}}{1-x} + 9x^9 \\ge \\frac{9/10 - 9^9/10^9}{1/10} + 9 \\cdot \\frac{9^{9}}{10^9} \\\\ &amp;= 9 - 10 \\cdot \\frac{9^9}{10^9} + 9 \\cdot \\frac{9^9}{10^9} = 9 - \\frac{9^9}{10^9} &gt; 8. \\end{align*}\" width=\"383\" height=\"89\" />\nSimilarly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/1/af1fdd1c9c151d28f320d685ba8e804116434177.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V(x) &gt; 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"20\" />.  It then follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/7/e375fcb7506e388abd2d43bbe2e5720165362463.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u, v \\in (0,9/10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Now, for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/8/f2814c6f6ef5bcdca44e299fbe3286f96eb48a6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in (0,9/10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/0/7b0965a08065dd3d4b7c4e1a8589d1da595cd56c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} V(x) &amp;= U(x) + V(x)-U(x) = U(x) + 10x^{11}+x^{10} -9x^9 \\\\ &amp;= U(x) + x^9 (10x -9) (x+1) &lt; U(x) . \\end{align*}\" width=\"446\" height=\"47\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> are both strictly increasing functions over the nonnegative reals, it then follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/e/ddeb36defeb65d2a05aa127bdc978a2ec1a4ef25.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[V(u) &lt; U(u) = 8 = V(v),\\]\" width=\"201\" height=\"18\" />\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/c/9ac520c83016d5022c055f0fe3089af59adba0cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u&lt;v$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"10\" />, as desired.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO\" title=\"1989 USAMO\">1989 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1989\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1989 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=356639#356639\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both